      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>Brain dump after the Papert Lab call. The thing I actually want, as a researcher:</div><div><br/></div><ol><li><b>Remember where a thought came from.</b> If I write "leakage is probably per-student", I want one click to the chat / paper / Slack message / run log where that came from.</li><li>Pull in what I already have: chats with Claude + ChatGPT, my Zotero PDFs, notes apps, repos. I'm not going to re-type anything.</li><li>Don't make me organize. Projects should emerge from the material (cluster by project, let me fix it).</li><li>Duplicates are the enemy: same paper from Zotero and Downloads should be ONE thing with two locations.</li><li>A canvas, not just a doc. Ideas next to their sources.</li><li>Works offline-ish, fast search.</li></ol><div><br/></div><div>Anti-goals</div><ul><li>not another second-brain template system.</li><li>not a chatbot over my files that makes things up. citations or nothing.</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Engelbart's "augmenting human intellect" is the frame. the notebook should make the trail visible.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
</en-export>
